KATARUNGANG PAMBARANGAY
A. PROCEDURE IN FILING COMPLAINTS

    Residents who wish to file a complaint may proceed to the Barangay Hall and follow the complaint filing procedure.

    Option 1: Filing a Complaint at the Barangay Hall
    Steps:
        Proceed to the Barangay Hall and log in to the record book, stating your purpose to the Officer of the Day.
        The OIC/Barangay Secretary records the complainant's complaint in the Book of Complaints and prepares the hearing schedule.
        The necessary notice and summons are prepared for service and signed by the Punong Barangay.
        The complainant pays the filing fee of ₱350.00 to the Barangay Treasurer and receives an Official Receipt.
        The notice is served to the complainant, while the summons is served to the respondent to inform them of the scheduled hearing.
        Option 2: Filing a Written Complaint Letter or Submitting a Police Blotter
    Steps:
        Prepare a complaint letter addressed to the Punong Barangay or submit a Police Blotter to the Barangay Hall.
        Proceed to the Barangay Hall and log in to the record book, stating your purpose to the Officer of the Day. Submit the complaint letter or Police Blotter.
        The OIC/Barangay Secretary records the complaint in the Book of Complaints and prepares the hearing schedule.
        The necessary notice and summons are prepared for service and signed by the Punong Barangay.
        The complainant pays the filing fee of ₱350.00 to the Barangay Treasurer and receives an Official Receipt.
        The notice is served to the complainant, while the summons is served to the respondent to inform them of the scheduled hearing.
    Fees:
        Complaint filing fee: ₱350.00.
B. CERTIFICATION TO FILE ACTION (CFA)

    The Certification to File Action (CFA) may be issued through either of the following procedures, depending on the authorized signatory.

    Option 1: Issued by the Pangkat Chairman
    Steps:
        Proceed to the Barangay Hall and log in to the record book, stating your purpose to the Officer of the Day.
        Submit a request to the Barangay Secretary for the preparation of the Certification to File Action.
        The Pangkat Chairman signs the prepared Certification to File Action.
        Pay the certification fee of ₱500.00 to the Barangay Treasurer.
        Receive the Official Receipt and claim the issued certification.
        Option 2: Issued by the Lupon Chairman
    Steps:
        Proceed to the Barangay Hall and log in to the record book, stating your purpose to the Officer of the Day.
        Submit a request to the Barangay Secretary for the preparation of the Certification to File Action.
        The Lupon Chairman signs the prepared Certification to File Action.
        Pay the certification fee of ₱500.00 to the Barangay Treasurer.
        Receive the Official Receipt and claim the issued certification.
    Fees:
        Certification to File Action fee: ₱500.00.

C. CERTIFICATION TO BAR ACTION (CBA)
    Steps:
        The respondent proceeds to the Barangay Hall and logs in to the record book, stating their purpose to the Officer of the Day.
        The respondent submits a request to the Barangay Secretary for the preparation of the Certification to Bar Action.
        The Lupon Chairman or Pangkat Chairman signs the prepared certification.
        The respondent pays the certification fee of ₱100.00 to the Barangay Treasurer.
        The respondent receives the Official Receipt and claims the issued certification.
    Fees:
        Certification to Bar Action fee: ₱100.00.

D. CERTIFICATE TO BAR COUNTER-CLAIM (CBC)
    Requirements:
        Proof of identity of the proper party.
    Steps:
        The complainant proceeds to the Barangay Hall and logs in to the record book, stating their purpose to the Officer of the Day.
        The complainant submits a request to the Barangay Secretary for the preparation of the Certificate to Bar Counter-Claim.
        The Lupon Chairman or Pangkat Chairman signs the prepared certification.
        The complainant pays the certification fee of ₱100.00 to the Barangay Treasurer.
        The complainant receives the Official Receipt and claims the issued Certificate to Bar Counter-Claim.
    Fees:
        Certificate to Bar Counter-Claim fee: ₱100.00.